<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson wins $20 mln Oman contract.</title>
<headline>Ericsson wins $20 mln Oman contract.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecoms group Ericsson said on Tuesday it had won a $20 million contract to expand the Global System for Mobile communications (GSM) network in Muscat, Oman.</p>
<p>The contract from the General Telecommunications Organisation, Ministry of PTT, includes Ericsson's switching system and radio base stations. Ericsson said in a statement that it also covered GSM features for data transmissions and services for operation and maintenance of the GSM network.</p>
<p>-- Belinda Goldsmith, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
